  "question": {
    "text": "A proton of mass ' $m_{\\mathrm{p}}$ ' has same energy as that of a photon of wavelength ' $\\lambda$ '. If the proton is moving at non-relativistic speed, then ratio of its de Broglie wavelength to the wavelength of photon is.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gWAkC",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{c}} \\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{E}}{\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{p}}}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZiIHC",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{c}} \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\mathrm{E}}{\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{p}}}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9TH5c",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2 c} \\sqrt{\\frac{E}{m_p}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BMIkn",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{c}} \\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{E}}{2 \\mathrm{~m}_{\\mathrm{p}}}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Energy of photon $=E=\\frac{h c}{\\lambda}$\n$\\Rightarrow$ Wavelength of photon $=\\lambda=\\frac{h c}{E}$\nEnergy of proton $=E=\\frac{1}{2} m_p v^2=\\frac{P^2}{2 m_p}$\n$\\Rightarrow$ Linear momentum of proton $=P=\\sqrt{2 m_p E}$\nOr de-Broglie wavelength of proton\n$\\begin{aligned}\n=\\lambda_p= & \\frac{h}{P}=\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{2 m_p E}} \\\\\n\\text { Ratio } \\frac{\\lambda_p}{\\lambda} & =\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{2 m_p E}} \\times \\frac{E}{h c} \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{c} \\sqrt{\\frac{E}{2 m_p}}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
